    <h2 class="sub">1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      We may collect personal information that you voluntarily provide to us when 
      you contact Ridgeway or submit an inquiry through our website.
    </p>
    <p>
      Depending on how you interact with us, this may include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Name</li>
      <li>Email address</li>
      <li>Phone number</li>
      <li>Company or organization name</li>
      <li>Project address or location</li>
      <li>Information about your project, construction needs, or services requested</li>
      <li>Any other information you choose to provide in a message or inquiry</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may also automatically collect limited technical information when you 
      visit our website, such as your IP address, browser type, device type, 
      pages visited, and general information about how visitors use the website. 
      This information may be collected through cookies, analytics, or similar 
      technologies if these tools are enabled on our website.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sub">2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>
      We collect and use personal information for reasonable business purposes, including to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Respond to inquiries and requests</li>
      <li>Contact you about a potential or existing project</li>
      <li>Understand your construction, renovation, maintenance, or other service requirements</li>
      <li>Prepare estimates, proposals, or scopes of work</li>
      <li>Provide and manage our services</li>
      <li>Communicate with clients, landlords, leasing agents, contractors, and other project partners</li>
      <li>Improve our website, services, and customer experience</li>
      <li>Maintain appropriate business and project records</li>
      <li>Protect the security and integrity of our website and systems</li>
      <li>Meet legal, regulatory, insurance, or contractual requirements</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We will not use personal information for a new purpose that is incompatible 
      with the purpose for which it was originally collected without obtaining 
      appropriate consent, unless otherwise permitted or required by law.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sub">3. Consent</h2>
    <p>
      Where required by applicable law, Ridgeway will obtain your consent before 
      collecting, using, or disclosing your personal information.
    </p>
    <p>
      By voluntarily submitting information through our website—for example, 
      by completing a contact form—you consent to Ridgeway collecting and using 
      that information for the purpose of responding to your inquiry and 
      communicating with you about the services or project you have asked us about.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may withdraw your consent to certain uses of your personal information, 
      subject to legal, contractual, or other reasonable restrictions. If you would 
      like to withdraw consent or ask us about how your information is being used, 
      please contact us using the information provided below.
    </p>
    <p>
      Canadian privacy guidance emphasizes that consent should be meaningful and 
      that people should understand what information is being collected, why it 
      is being collected, and with whom it may be shared.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sub">4. Information We Share</h2>
    <p>
      Ridgeway does not sell or rent your personal information.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may disclose personal information when reasonably necessary to operate 
      our business and provide our services. This may include sharing information 
      with:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Service providers who assist us with website hosting, form processing, email, information technology, or other business functions</li>
      <li>Contractors, consultants, trades, engineers, designers, or other project partners when necessary to provide requested services or manage a project</li>
      <li>Professional advisors, such as legal, accounting, insurance, or financial professionals</li>
      <li>Government authorities, regulators, courts, or law enforcement where required or permitted by law</li>
      <li>Other parties where you have provided consent or where disclosure is otherwise permitted or required by law</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We expect third-party service providers handling personal information on our behalf to use appropriate safeguards and to handle information only for authorized purposes.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sub">5. Website Forms and Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      Our website may use third-party services to operate contact forms, 
      host website content, provide analytics, or support other website functions.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we use a third-party service to process information submitted through a 
      website form, the information you provide may be transmitted to and 
      processed by that service in accordance with its own privacy practices.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our website may also use analytics or similar technologies to understand 
      website traffic and improve the site.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sub">6. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
    <p>
      Our website may use cookies or similar technologies to support website 
      functionality, understand website usage, or improve the user experience.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cookies are small files that may be stored on your device when you visit a website.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can manage cookies through your browser settings, and you may choose to 
      disable cookies if you prefer. However, some website features may not 
      function properly if cookies are disabled.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sub">7. Retention of Personal Information</h2>
    <p>
      We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary to 
      fulfill the purposes for which it was collected, provide our services, 
      maintain appropriate business records, resolve disputes, protect our 
      legitimate business interests, or meet legal, regulatory, insurance, or 
      contractual requirements.
    </p>
    <p>
      When personal information is no longer required, we take reasonable steps 
      to securely delete, destroy, or anonymize it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sub">8. Protecting Your Information</h2>
    <p>
      Ridgeway takes reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards 
      to protect personal information against loss, theft, unauthorized access, 
      disclosure, copying, use, modification, or destruction.
    </p>
    <p>
      The safeguards we use may include appropriate access controls, passwords, 
      secure systems, physical protections, and limiting access to personal 
      information to individuals who need it for legitimate business purposes.
    </p>
    <p>
      No method of transmitting or storing information electronically can be
      guaranteed to be completely secure. While we take reasonable measures to 
      protect information, we cannot guarantee absolute security.
    </p>
    <p>
      Canadian privacy guidance requires safeguards appropriate to the sensitivity 
      of the information being protected.
    </p>

    <h2 class="sub">9. Information Provided by You</h2>
